## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where users tailing a custom Voice Call JSONL log with `voicecall tail --file <path>` could see follow-mode output skip newly appended bytes, split a record, or corrupt a UTF-8 character when the file was read across filesystem boundaries.

## Why This Change Was Made

The custom-log tailer now advances by the actual byte count returned from `fs.readSync`, keeps streaming UTF-8 decoder state, and emits only complete newline-terminated records across both the initial file read and later follow reads. The SQLite-backed `calls.jsonl` history path is unchanged.

## User Impact

Voice Call provider/debug log tails keep following appended custom log lines without silently jumping past unread bytes, printing half-records, or corrupting split UTF-8 characters.

## Evidence

- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/voice-call/src/cli.test.ts` - 1 file, 12 tests passed.
- Real CLI boundary fallback: `node --import tsx proof-live.mjs` imports the production `registerVoiceCallCli`, runs `voicecall tail --file custom.log`, and injects filesystem-boundary short reads or startup partial bytes.
- Negative controls: short-read cases report `short-read-triggered: true`; startup cases report `short-read-triggered: false`; all cases report `printed-expected-lines: true`, `emitted-replacement-character: false`, and `emitted-partial-fragment: false`.

```text
$ node --import tsx proof-live.mjs
entrypoint: registerVoiceCallCli voicecall tail --file custom.log
case: newline
short-read-triggered: true
printed-expected-lines: true
emitted-replacement-character: false
emitted-partial-fragment: false
raw-output: "first\nsecond\n"
case: mid-record
short-read-triggered: true
printed-expected-lines: true
emitted-replacement-character: false
emitted-partial-fragment: false
raw-output: "{\"event\":\"first\"}\n{\"event\":\"second\"}\n"
case: multibyte
short-read-triggered: true
printed-expected-lines: true
emitted-replacement-character: false
emitted-partial-fragment: false
raw-output: "{\"word\":\"café\"}\n"
case: startup-record
short-read-triggered: false
printed-expected-lines: true
emitted-replacement-character: false
emitted-partial-fragment: false
raw-output: "{\"event\":\"start\"}\n"
case: startup-multibyte
short-read-triggered: false
printed-expected-lines: true
emitted-replacement-character: false
emitted-partial-fragment: false
raw-output: "{\"word\":\"café\"}\n"
```

